---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy of Lab to Prod and of the lab-to-prod publishing app.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Last updated 13 November 2026.</p>

    <h2>This blog</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a static blog hosted on GitHub Pages. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics script
      and has no forms or accounts. GitHub, as the host, may keep standard server logs; see the GitHub
      privacy statement.
    </p>

    <h2>The lab-to-prod publishing app</h2>
    <p>
      The author runs a small open-source app, lab-to-prod, that posts his own notes to his own
      accounts (Facebook Page, LinkedIn, YouTube and DEV). It signs in only to the author's accounts,
      with the permissions those posts need: uploading and scheduling videos and captions, publishing
      posts, and reading the view and reaction counts of those posts.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>It does not collect, sell or share data about anyone else.</li>
      <li>Access tokens are stored as encrypted GitHub Actions secrets and are never published.</li>
      <li>The only data it keeps is a public record of what was posted where and daily post counts,
        in the open-source repository.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To revoke access, remove the app from the connected-apps settings of the account concerned
      (for Google: myaccount.google.com/permissions).
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy: open an issue in the lab-to-prod repository on GitHub.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
